iver Godāvarī, the lovely Lakşmana, performing his bath, and securing lotuses and fruits, came back (to the asylum).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-15-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3014022","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7a55a5614936485fac29afe48a99aab546423feef63f92b7f283fa10acc95e6d","compact":"d5b2ffdf4c47bddd2f590cf6722adc044115aa3bb705ab12ee3995a1a1f7b810","nasal":"6cac8c4c26c5df9b44ec991d8898eb96ef58d3511280dae9d19f94d15503f7d3"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-14-23","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":14,"verse":23,"english":"Then offering flowers, and duly performing rites for the peace (of the habitation), Lakşmaņa showed the asylum which he had made to Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-15-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3014023","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"83cf7349486c13b0e1475d53963fac96b5a4d6e216fa4c146deb455d3d8e8c04","compact":"ceca23f50c8e8fb90b07c3a821c9da94c926eccf7961639b15fc4ed54ed70a2c","nasal":"978cb4cbc90400a40e9af8f6fc82ec42719b05a1dcae9ec1f3c7ab33a57fb1d4"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-14-24","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":14,"verse":24,"english":"Seeing the beautiful asylum along with Sitā, Rāghava experienced high raptures.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-15-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3014024","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9cc54be93b831e0bdc3558723bdfcf05e3679e1e8a7da42b09171a6805998c3d","compact":"6062e85d02adc1b84bb727d786ae4b14c6960956faccf6005ead06467d12164e","nasal":"6062e85d02adc1b84bb727d786ae4b14c6960956faccf6005ead06467d12164e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-14-25","kanda":3,"kandaId